# Before: the Result captured this successful witness statement, but the new
# StmtResult-to-Lean compiler rejected the whole WitnessNonemptySet family and
# its ListSetMembership builtin certificate.
#
# Now: the statement combines its ordered local proof-step Results with its
# final membership Result inside one inherited compiler environment. The
# membership proof wraps the exact equality child selected by index 0; only
# the outer nonempty-set FactId is published after the environment is popped.
#
# Boundary: a function-set witness has a different final nonempty-return-set
# check and stays fail-closed until that separate Result shape is implemented.
# An out-of-range selected list index is rejected by a focused Rust test.
witness $is_nonempty_set({1, 2}) from 1
